{"input_text": "Question: How would I calculate the power series of $f(x)$ if $f(f(x)) = e^x$?  Is there a faster-converging method than power series for fractional iteration/functional square roots? 

Answer: There is a lot of material about this question here and in mathoverflow. There is also a "Tetration forum", where someone has implemented a version of tetration due to Hellmuth Kneser, see some forum entries there:  http://math.eretrandre.org/tetrationforum/forumdisplay.php?fid=8 " also in citizendium there is an extensive article of Dmitri Kousznetzov who claims he has a usable interpretation (and implementation) see  http://en.citizendium.org/wiki/Tetration 
