Answer: As Michael Hardy noted in comments, the likely problem is that you are trying to model  the process with inappropriate distribution. If a confidence interval is built using a distribution supported on positive numbers, it will consist of positive numbers. Given the context of "pings", it is reasonable to try the  exponential distribution , which is often used to model the waiting time. Another possibility is  log-normal distribution  also mentioned by Michael Hardy.  
