Indeed, we $\large never$ do Montecarlo with $\ds{\int_{0}^{1}x^{2}\,\dd x}$. We make the following transformation such that the integrand becomes closer to a smooth function:
$$
\int_{0}^{1}x^{2}\,\dd x
=\half\bracks{\int_{0}^{1}x^{2}\,\dd x + \int_{0}^{1}\pars{1 - x}^{2}\,\dd x}
=\int_{0}^{1}\bracks{x\pars{x - 1} + \half}\,\dd x
$$

