{"input_text": "Question: Given $m$, $a$ and $b$ are very big numbers, how do you calculate $ (a*b)\pmod m$ ?  
 As they are very big number I can not calculate $(a*b)$ directly. So I need another method. 

Answer: You can exploit the binary representation of these two numbers.
Suppose we have to multiply (a*b)%c where 0<=a,b,c<=10^18.
Then we can use this method: 
 ull mulmod(ull a,ull b,ull c){
    if(a<=1000000000ULL && b<=1000000000ULL){
        ull ret = ((a%c)*(b%c))%c;
        return ret;
    }
    ull ret = 0ULL, a=a%c;
    while(b > 0ULL){
        if(b&1ULL) {
            ret = (ret+a)%c;
        }
        a = (a<<1ULL)%c;
        b>>=1ULL;
    }
    return ret%c;
}

 Hope this helps ! 
